          },
          "format": 0,
          "queryType": "sql",
          "meta": {},
          "rawSql": "SELECT ts AS time, cast(sum(value) AS DOUBLE) AS \"Total Consumption\"\nFROM cel_community_energy\nWHERE $__timeFilter(ts)\n  AND community_id = '101110-002726'\n  AND segment = 'total'\n  AND direction = 'consumption'\nSAMPLE BY $__sampleByInterval FILL(NULL)\nORDER BY time",
          "refId": "A",
          "selectedFormat": 0
        }
      ],
      "title": "Total Consumption",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Returns the per-bucket series and lets the panel's reduceOptions sum it: the stat panel's graphMode:area sparkline needs the series, not a pre-reduced scalar. Keys off segment ('cel'/'grid'/'total') rather than product_code -- the same distinction under the name the parser stores, so it survives a provider-side encoding change (see classify_metric_type in models.py)."
    },
